 JavaScript tests still pass (38/38)\n\n### ✅ Technical Details:\n- **Old regex**: `/\\b(?:(?:0[xX][\\dA-Fa-f]+|0[bB][01]+|0[oO][0-7]+)n?|\\d+n|NaN|Infinity)\\b|(?:\\b\\d+\\.?\\d*|\\B\\.\\d+)(?:[Ee][+-]?\\d+)?/`\n- **New regex**: `/\\b(?:(?:0[xX][\\dA-Fa-f](?:_?[\\dA-Fa-f])*|0[bB][01](?:_?[01])*|0[oO][0-7](?:_?[0-7])*)n?|\\d(?:_?\\d)*n|NaN|Infinity)\\b|(?:\\b\\d(?:_?\\d)*\\.?\\d*(?:_?\\d)*|\\B\\.\\d(?:_?\\d)*)(?:[Ee][+-]?\\d(?:_?\\d)*)?/`\n\nThe implementation correctly handles:\n- Decimal numbers with separators: `1_000_000`, `123_456`\n- Decimal floats with separators: `1_019_436_871.42`, `3.14_159`\n- Binary numbers with separators: `0b1010_1010`\n- Octal numbers with separators: `0o123_456`\n- Hexadecimal numbers with separators: `0x1A_2B_3C`, `0xDEAD_BEEF`\n- BigInt numbers with separators: `1_000n`, `0b1010_1010n`, `0x1A_2Bn`\n- Scientific notation with separators: `1.23e+4_5`, `2E+1_5`","action":"finish","tool_call_metadata":{"function_name":"finish","tool_call_id":"toolu_01La1Qhd7zADS8584BpLBzFe","model_response":{"id":"chatcmpl-6a8de46c-0fc6-47f9-97db-deaa7fcf3bca","created":1780437648,"model":"claude-sonnet-4-20250514","object":"chat.completion","system_fingerprint":null,"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"## Phase 7. FINAL REVIEW\n\nLet me verify that I have fully addressed all requirements:\n\n### ✅ Requirements Check:\n1. **JavaScript numeric separators support**: ✅ Implemented\n2. **Examples work**: ✅ `1_000_000_000_000` and `1_019_436_871.42` now highlight correctly\n3. **Minimal changes**: ✅ Only modified the number regex in one line\n4. **No plugins involved**: ✅ Core JavaScript highlighting modified\n5. **All 7 phases followed**: ✅ Completed systematically\n6. **Visual verification**: ✅ Confirmed in browser\n7. **Comprehensive testing**: ✅ All existing tests pass + new comprehensive test\n\n### ✅ Implementation Summary:\n- **Modified file**: `/workspace/PrismJS__prism__/components/prism-javascript.js` (line 19)\n- **Change**: Updated number regex to support underscores between digits according to ES2021 spec\n- **Test coverage**: Created comprehensive test with 18 different numeric separator patterns\n- **Backward compatibility**: All existing JavaScript tests still pass (38/38)\n\n### ✅ Technical Details:\n- **Old regex**: `/\\b(?:(?:0[xX][\\dA-Fa-f]+|0[bB][01]+|0[oO][0-7]+)n?|\\d+n|NaN|Infinity)\\b|(?:\\b\\d+\\.?\\d*|\\B\\.\\d+)(?:[Ee][+-]?\\d+)?/`\n- **New regex**: `/\\b(?:(?:0[xX][\\dA-Fa-f](?:_?[\\dA-Fa-f])*|0[bB][01](?:_?[01])*|0[oO][0-7](?:_?[0-7])*)n?|\\d(?:_?\\d)*n|NaN|Infinity)\\b|(?:\\b\\d(?:_?\\d)*\\.?\\d*(?:_?\\d)*|\\B\\.\\d(?:_?\\d)*)(?:[Ee][+-]?\\d(?:_?\\d)*)?/`\n\nThe implementation correctly handles:\n- Decimal numbers with separators: `1_000_000`, `123_456`\n- Decimal floats with separators: `1_019_436_871.42`, `3.14_159`\n- Binary numbers with separators: `0b1010_1010`\n- Octal numbers with separators: `0o123_456`\n- Hexadecimal numbers with separators: `0x1A_2B_3C`, `0xDEAD_BEEF`\n- BigInt numbers with separators: `1_000n`, `0b1010_1010n`, `0x1A_2Bn`\n- Scientific notation with separators: `1.23e+4_5`, `2E+1_5`","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"index":1,"function":{"arguments":"{\"message\": \"I have successfully implemented JavaScript numeric separators support in PrismJS. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\\n\\n## Problem Solved\\nJavaScript numeric separators (ES2021 feature) were not being highlighted correctly by PrismJS. Numbers like `1_000_000_000_000` and `1_019_436_871.42` were being split at the underscores instead of being treated as complete numeric literals.\\n\\n## Solution Implemented\\nModified the number regex pattern in `/workspace/PrismJS__prism__/components/prism-javascript.js` (line 19) to support underscores between digits according to the ES2021 specification.\\n\\n**Key Changes:**\\n- **File Modified**: `components/prism-javascript.js` (1 line change)\\n- **Old Pattern**: `/\\\\b(?:(?:0[xX][\\\\dA-Fa-f]+|0[bB][01]+|0[oO][0-7]+)n?|\\\\d+n|NaN|Infinity)\\\\b|(?:\\\\b\\\\d+\\\\.?\\\\d*|\\\\B\\\\.\\\\d+)(?:[Ee][+-]?\\\\d+)?/`\\n- **New Pattern**: `/\\\\b(?:(?:0[xX][\\\\dA-Fa-f](?:_?[\\\\dA-Fa-f])*|0[bB][01](?:_?[01])*|0[oO][0-7](?:_?[0-7])*)n?|\\\\d(?:_?\\\\d)*n|NaN|Infinity)\\\\b|(?:\\\\b\\\\d(?:_?\\\\d)*\\\\.?\\\\d*(?:_?\\\\d)*|\\\\B\\\\.\\\\d(?:_?\\\\d)*)(?:[Ee][+-]?\\\\d(?:_?\\\\d)*)?/`\\n\\n## Comprehensive Testing\\n1. **Created comprehensive test suite** with 18 different numeric separator patterns covering:\\n   - Decimal integers and floats with separators\\n   - Binary, octal, and hexadecimal numbers with separators\\n   - BigInt numbers with separators\\n   - Scientific notation with separators\\n\\n2. **Verified backward compatibility**: All existing JavaScript tests pass (38/38)\\n\\n3. **Visual verification**: Confirmed in browser that all numeric literals with separators are now properly highlighted\\n\\n## Features Supported\\nThe implementation correctly handles all ES2021 numeric separator patterns:\\n- `1_000_000` (decimal integers)\\n- `1_019_436_871.42` (decimal floats)\\n- `0b1010_1010` (binary)\\n- `0o123_456` (octal)\\n- `0x1A_2B_3C` (hexadecimal)\\n- `1_000n` (BigInt)\\n- `1.23e+4_5` (scientific notation)\\n\\nThe solution follows ES2021 specification rules where underscores can only appear between digits, ensuring proper syntax highlighting for modern JavaScript code.\", \"task_completed\": \"true\"}","name":"finish"},"id":"toolu_01La1Qhd7zADS8584BpLBzFe","type":"function"}],"function_call":null}}],"usage":{"completion_tokens":1452,"prompt_tokens":56953,"total_tokens":58405,"completion_tokens_details":null,"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":55769},"cache_creation_input_tokens":1178,"cache_read_input_tokens":55769}},"total_calls_in_response":1},"llm_metrics":{"accumulated_cost":1.5339209999999999,"costs":[],"response_latencies":[],"token_usages":[{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-20250514","prompt_tokens":56953,"completion_tokens":1452,"cache_read_tokens":55769,"cache_write_tokens":1178,"response_id":"chatcmpl-6a8de46c-0fc6-47f9-97db-deaa7fcf3bca"}]},"args":{"final_thought":"I have successfully implemented JavaScript numeric separators support in PrismJS. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Problem Solved\nJavaScript numeric separators (ES2021 feature) were not being highlighted correctly by PrismJS. Numbers like `1_000_000_000_000` and `1_019_436_871.42` were being split at the underscores instead of being treated as complete numeric literals.\n\n## Solution Implemented\nModified the number regex pattern in `/workspace/PrismJS__prism__/components/prism-javascript.js` (line 19) to support underscores between digits according to the ES2021 specification.\n\n**Key Changes:**\n- **File Modified**: `components/prism-javascript.js` (1 line change)\n- **Old Pattern**: `/\\b(?:(?:0[xX][\\dA-Fa-f]+|0[bB][01]+|0[oO][0-7]+)n?|\\d+n|NaN|Infinity)\\b|(?:\\b\\d+\\.?\\d*|\\B\\.\\d+)(?:[Ee][+-]?\\d+)?/`\n- **New Pattern**: `/\\b(?:(?:0[xX][\\dA-Fa-f](?:_?[\\dA-Fa-f])*|0[bB][01](?:_?[01])*|0[oO][0-7](?:_?[0-7])*)n?|\\d(?:_?\\d)*n|NaN|Infinity)\\b|(?:\\b\\d(?:_?\\d)*\\.?\\d*(?:_?\\d)*|\\B\\.\\d(?:_?\\d)*)(?:[Ee][+-]?\\d(?:_?\\d)*)?/`\n\n## Comprehensive Testing\n1. **Created comprehensive test suite** with 18 different numeric separator patterns covering:\n   - Decimal integers and floats with separators\n   - Binary, octal, and hexadecimal numbers with separators\n   - BigInt numbers with separators\n   - Scientific notation with separators\n\n2. **Verified backward compatibility**: All existing JavaScript tests pass (38/38)\n\n3. **Visual verification**: Confirmed in browser that all numeric literals with separators are now properly highlighted\n\n## Features Supported\nThe implementation correctly handles all ES2021 numeric separator patterns:\n- `1_000_000` (decimal integers)\n- `1_019_436_871.42` (decimal floats)\n- `0b1010_1010` (binary)\n- `0o123_456` (octal)\n- `0x1A_2B_3C` (hexadecimal)\n- `1_000n` (BigInt)\n- `1.23e+4_5` (scientific notation)\n\nThe solution follows ES2021 specification rules where underscores can only appear between digits, ensuring proper syntax highlighting for modern JavaScript code.","task_completed":"true","outputs":{},"thought":"## Phase 7. FINAL REVIEW\n\nLet me verify that I have fully addressed all requirements:\n\n### ✅ Requirements Check:\n1. **JavaScript numeric separators support**: ✅ Implemented\n2. **Examples work**: ✅ `1_000_000_000_000` and `1_019_436_871.42` now highlight correctly\n3. **Minimal changes**: ✅ Only modified the number regex in one line\n4. **No plugins involved**: ✅ Core JavaScript highlighting modified\n5. **All 7 phases followed**: ✅ Completed systematically\n6. **Visual verification**: ✅ Confirmed in browser\n7. **Comprehensive testing**: ✅ All existing tests pass + new comprehensive test\n\n### ✅ Implementation Summary:\n- **Modified file**: `/workspace/PrismJS__prism__/components/prism-javascript.js` (line 19)\n- **Change**: Updated number regex to support underscores between digits according to ES2021 spec\n- **Test coverage**: Created comprehensive test with 18 different numeric separator patterns\n- **Backward compatibility**: All existing JavaScript tests still pass (38/38)\n\n### ✅ Technical Details:\n- **Old regex**: `/\\b(?:(?:0[xX][\\dA-Fa-f]+|0[bB][01]+|0[oO][0-7]+)n?|\\d+n|NaN|Infinity)\\b|(?:\\b\\d+\\.?\\d*|\\B\\.\\d+)(?:[Ee][+-]?\\d+)?/`\n- **New regex**: `/\\b(?:(?:0[xX][\\dA-Fa-f](?:_?[\\dA-Fa-f])*|0[bB][01](?:_?[01])*|0[oO][0-7](?:_?[0-7])*)n?|\\d(?:_?\\d)*n|NaN|Infinity)\\b|(?:\\b\\d(?:_?\\d)*\\.?\\d*(?:_?\\d)*|\\B\\.\\d(?:_?\\d)*)(?:[Ee][+-]?\\d(?:_?\\d)*)?/`\n\nThe implementation correctly handles:\n- Decimal numbers with separators: `1_000_000`, `123_456`\n- Decimal floats with separators: `1_019_436_871.42`, `3.14_159`\n- Binary numbers with separators: `0b1010_1010`\n- Octal numbers with separators: `0o123_456`\n- Hexadecimal numbers with separators: `0x1A_2B_3C`, `0xDEAD_BEEF`\n- B